:: Help Company Actions [nobr] {"position":"825,4125"}
<p>The panel at the bottom right is the only part of the dashboard that makes time pass. It has two halves: the <b>Work</b> card on the left decides how long you work, the list on the right holds everything else worth doing right now. They are the same shortcuts as the <a href="#" data-help="Help Time And Actions">quick links</a> in the sidebar, which the desk hides. Each one only shows up when it makes sense, and says what it costs.</p>
<p>Time always passes one action at a time, even when a button spends several at once: every action lets your scheduled tasks start and finish on time and gives your employees one action of project work. Then the dashboard refreshes. You can click anywhere on a button or row.</p>

<h3>The Work card</h3>
<p>The card always has the same four tiles. A tile that has nothing to do right now is greyed out and says why.</p>
<p>While you work, every requirement of every active project goes up by <b>1</b> per action (never past what it needs). Your employees also contribute, but only for actions inside work hours.</p>
<ul>
	<li><b>One action</b>: always there. You work for one action.</li>
	<li><b>Until work starts</b>: on a weekday before the work day. You just wait, without working.</li>
	<li><b>Until her task</b>: a <a href="#" data-help="Help Company Tasks">task with you</a> is scheduled for later today. You work until the action it starts on, then you are where it needs you, and she asks you right away. If it takes place in another room of the office, you walk over at the end without spending an extra action.</li>
	<li><b>Until her task is done</b>: a task of $mom.callName or $sister.callName is running. You work until it ends (the first one, if both have one running).</li>
	<li><b>Until the end of the work day</b>: during work hours on a weekday. You work through every action that is left of the work day. Tasks in the <a href="#" data-help="Help Company Schedule">schedule</a> run exactly as they would if you clicked through.</li>
</ul>
<div class="help-note">Each button names the time slot it takes you to. A task with you still needs her energy to start: if she is too tired by then, she doesn't come, and you just spent the time working.</div>

<h3>The list</h3>
<p>Whatever else you can do from the desk right now, the most urgent one on top and lit up. For example: heading to the place of a quest that is ready, joining her when a task with you has started in another room and she is waiting (free, so you still make it in time), hearing about her day, going home, or going to bed at night. Going somewhere never costs time here.</p>

<h3>Calling them to your desk</h3>
<p>While $mom.callName or $sister.callName is in the office, her card under employees has a small phone button. Calling her costs no time and opens the <a href="#" data-help="Help Npc Interaction">interaction screen</a> with her. Whatever you do there costs what it always costs.</p>
